<title>BELGIUM: Iomega, Siemens in notebook Zip drive accord.</title>
<headline>Iomega, Siemens in notebook Zip drive accord.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Siemens Nixdorf is to provide Iomega's new notebook Zip drive as an option in its new series of notebook PCs, Iomega International SA, a unit of Iomega Corp, said in a statement dated July 17.</p>
<p>This makes the German company the first European computer manufacturer to integrate Iomega's new notebook Zip drive into its product range, Iomega said. The notebook Zip drives are due to be made available in the second half of 1997.</p>
<p>Iomega said separately that global shipments of the firm's data storage drives had reached 10 million, including more than seven million Zip drives.</p>
